           File containing ssccrriipptt's terminal input.

       --OO, ----lloogg--oouutt _f_i_l_e
           File containing ssccrriipptt's terminal output.

       --BB, ----lloogg--iioo _f_i_l_e
           File containing ssccrriipptt's terminal output and input.

       --tt, ----ttiimmiinngg _f_i_l_e
           File containing ssccrriipptt's timing output. This option overrides
           old-style arguments.

       --TT, ----lloogg--ttiimmiinngg _f_i_l_e
           This is an alias for --tt, maintained for compatibility with
           ssccrriipptt(1) command-line options.

       --ss, ----ttyyppeessccrriipptt _f_i_l_e
           File containing ssccrriipptt's terminal output. Deprecated alias to
           ----lloogg--oouutt. This option overrides old-style arguments.

       --cc, ----ccrr--mmooddee _m_o_d_e
           Specifies how to use the CR (0x0D, carriage return) character from
           log files. The default mode is _a_u_t_o, in this case CR is replaced
           with line break for stdin log, because otherwise ssccrriippttrreeppllaayy would
           overwrite the same line. The other modes are _n_e_v_e_r and _a_l_w_a_y_s.

       --dd, ----ddiivviissoorr _n_u_m_b_e_r
           Speed up the replay displaying this _n_u_m_b_e_r of times. The argument
           is a floating-point number. It’s called divisor because it divides
           the timings by this factor. This option overrides old-style
           arguments.

       --mm, ----mmaaxxddeellaayy _n_u_m_b_e_r
           Set the maximum delay between updates to _n_u_m_b_e_r of seconds. The
           argument is a floating-point number. This can be used to avoid long
           pauses in the typescript replay.

       ----ssuummmmaarryy
           Display details about the session recorded in the specified timing
           file and exit. The session has to be recorded using _a_d_v_a_n_c_e_d format
           (see ssccrriipptt(1) option ----llooggggiinngg--ffoorrmmaatt for more details).

       --xx, ----ssttrreeaamm _t_y_p_e
           Forces ssccrriippttrreeppllaayy to print only the specified stream. The
           supported stream types are _i_n, _o_u_t, _s_i_g_n_a_l, or _i_n_f_o. This option is
           recommended for multi-stream logs (e.g., ----lloogg--iioo) in order to
           print only specified data.

       --hh, ----hheellpp
           Display help text and exit.

       --VV, ----vveerrssiioonn
           Print version and exit.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
           % script --log-timing file.tm --log-out script.out
